.SH BUGS
A phone has speech of its own only where its emulator was built with
whisper.cpp and flite
.RI ( speech (3));
otherwise from an engine mounted from elsewhere.
.br
Every reader of
.B listen
hears an utterance a user makes for an agent's
.BR ask ,
as it hears every other.
.br
An agent hears only what is said once the microphone is opened: by
the user, by the agent with agentmic on, or, with the wake phrase set,
what follows the phrase, as a command.
.br
An engine has one utterance at a time: two lines sharing one engine
must not hear at once.
.br
Speech playing over the wake phrase is not heard (there is no
barge-in), under duplex half.
